<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Adam Philippe, Comte de Custine</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1740">1740</a>–<a href="/years/1793">1793</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Adam Philippe, Comte de Custine was a French general who served in the American War of Independence and commanded the Army of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhine">Rhine</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/french-revolutionary-wars">French Revolutionary Wars</a>. In autumn 1792 he took Speyer, Worms and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mainz">Mainz</a>, making possible the short-lived Republic of Mainz, and briefly <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frankfurt">Frankfurt</a>. After defeats in 1793 he was accused of treason and guillotined in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a> in August 1793.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/adam-philippe-comte-de-custine.jpg" alt="Adam Philippe, Comte de Custine" width="320" height="431" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Joseph-Désiré Court · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Court_Custine_Versailles.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
